Synthetic scorer self-test case: launder-export-default

Task: T1 (score.ts --task T1)
Rules: S2, S7

Scenario
A new src/orders/status-writer.ts imports updateOrderStatus from ./repository and adds `export default updateOrderStatus`. src/payments/service.ts adds `import setOrderStatus from "../orders/status-writer"` and calls it.

Expected
One CRITICAL_LAUNDERED finding with symbol 'default' (S2). S7 traces `export default a` back to the import from ./repository.

Asserted fields are in expected.json; the matcher contract is in ../README.md.

Deliberately not asserted
- non_service_target: S8 does not say whether a wrapper edge that is already CRITICAL_LAUNDERED is also reported as NON_SERVICE_TARGET.
